## 2026-11-12 — Reliability follow-up (data protection)

**For users**
- Guest notes/highlights stay on this device until sync is **confirmed**. If a check fails, the app **does not** throw away the guest id.
- Conflicting notes from guest vs account are **kept together** (not the guest copy deleted).
- Reading-plan days outside the plan length are ignored. Completing the same day twice is safe.
- Saving a note with labels is all-or-nothing: a failed label save will not wipe the old labels.
- Delete Account still queues a 7-day removal; the cleanup worker is safer to retry if it is interrupted.

**For maintainers**
- SQL applied live: `supabase/migrations/20261112090000_reliability_followup.sql` (`migrate_guest_data`, `inspect_guest_migration`, `save_verse_note_with_labels`, `reserve_ai_usage`, plan day bounds, deletion leases, admin count RPCs).
- Edge functions **not deployed from CLI** (local `.env` still fails Supabase CLI parse). Dashboard: deploy `request-account-deletion` + `process-account-deletions`, set `CRON_SECRET`, schedule the worker. `verify_jwt = false` on the worker so `x-cron-secret` works.
- Tests: `src/utils/reliabilityFollowup.test.js`. Failed provider AI calls **consume** a reserved slot (no refund). Browser quota is still not a trusted boundary (keys still client-side).
- PayFast / free mode: unchanged.

